From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:01:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] 0001 CHOP: a second SAMPLE page that turns the pads
 into sample-start markers

New mod mods/0001-chop (enabled = false; excludes 0004 and 0008) and the
`make chop` (0000 0001 0002 0003) and `make chop-min` (0000 0001) targets.

Press SAMPLE twice for the CHOP page: PAD 1..12, STA 0..120 (that pad's
marker), CHP OFF/ON (ON latches the selected track, never the FX track).
While CHOP is on, pad k sets the chop track's STA to marker k through
param_set_value(set, 43, V<<8, T, 1, 1) - the call a STA knob turn ends in,
so live REC makes a stock STA p-lock - then the pad id in the UI message is
rewritten to the chop track and stock plays it as a normal pad hit. Note-offs
get the same rewrite. RAM-only state at the end of the `cave` claim.

Hooks: 0008's four page gates, a SAMPLE key gate (the SAMP view never hands a
plain press/release to the base page cycle), UI-loop cases 3 and 4, and a
held-trig lock-path guard so CHOP knobs never write a p-lock. Expect bytes
re-read from build/stock_mainos.bin. Both builds PASS verify in the guest
(bootstrap unchanged, null repack). Never run on hardware: test card in
design.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
