From d9b0302e26973c2701dcb10b8be48eec8e57bdff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:05:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] Sample Focus step 3: knob ids proven dead, END and DIV
 (D19, D20)

- Knob ids: 11..14 proven dead (Error-class ROM record, on no stock page,
  RAM record built like ids 3..5's, no reference into the ROM record, skipped
  by the boot CC/NRPN/container map builder, no constant-id direct call in 82
  call sites). Id 7 rejected: its CC 92 / NRPN 1:104 are the manual's Active
  Scene. Knob H will use id 2 instead. Proof in the registry note.
- One dispatcher, chop_knob (id -> knob via a 16-byte table), in the get,
  delta, text and lock gates; chop_value and the popup text cover all knobs.
- D END (id 11): right on, left off. A pad hit with END on sets the chop
  track's END to the next marker above its own (else 120) after STA, record 1;
  the step lock also locks END on each held step when id 44 is lockable
