From 449b935670e46cf22ff356fa55dd282015e2c088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:08:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] Sample Focus step 4: RND, random markers on held steps
 (D20)

- G RND (id 14, proven dead in step 3): turned while trig key(s) of the chop
  track are held, lock_gate sends it to chop_rnd_held, which runs the step lock
  (chop_held_with: the same six guards and stock hold sequence) with the
  invoker chop_rnd_step: each held step gets STA = a random marker 0..DIV-1
  (and END = its slice end when END is on and id 44 is lockable). Each detent
  re-rolls. CHOP off, or no trig held: nothing. Never a stock p-lock for id 14.
- The random index: shared_rnd (0000-shared) on CHOP's own LCG word chop_rng,
  N = 32767, made 0..65534, divu by DIV, remainder. 0001 now requires the
  shared runtime ([requires] shared = true, includes build/shared.inc).
- The strings move to cave2 (constants; the ROM patches follow by
  from_symbol), freeing cave for the hot path.

Guest: make samplefocus, chop-min, control, verify, random PASS. CHOP: .text
1132 B in cave (100 free), .cave2 919 B; 0 bytes changed in the bootstrap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
