Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Sample Focus step 5: LAY, lay the slices out on empty
 steps (D20)

- F LAY (id 13, proven dead in step 3): turned right, with CHOP on, the chop
  track selected, euclid off and STA lockable, it puts n = min(DIV, length)
  slices on steps s_i = i*length/n. Only an EMPTY step (step_flag_test mask 1
  clear, the same test that makes stock's grid trig key create) gets a trig
  (trig_create, as the trig key) plus its STA p-lock (and END with END on and
  id 44 lockable). A step that holds a trig is never touched. Then
  view_refresh_request(view), as the trig key after its create. Left: nothing.
- re/symbols.toml: step_flag_test 0x400bcaa0, trig_create 0x400bf6c0,
  view_refresh_request 0x40076c4c; the pattern_step_has_trig note now says
  what it really returns (r5c skeptic P4).

Guest: make samplefocus, chop-min, control, verify, random PASS. CHOP: .text
1132 B in cave (100 free), .cave2 1277 B; 0 bytes changed in the bootstrap.

